// name :
"P1756389842" "A Web of Intrigue"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Retaliation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P70370049" "It was retaliation!"
// DetailString :
"P2314259078" "After the battle in the Council base, the base's defeated leader spat out the following under interrogation: <br><br>'We did what we had to do to even the battle. Our counter-attack was provoked by the outages of Arachnos! It was retaliation, pure and simple! We will not allow Arachnos to steal from our computer network without consequence! <br>For Arakhn! <br>For Requiem! <br>And all for the Center!'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Retaliation2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4060232254" "You guys started it!"
// DetailString :
"P3268771558" "After you defeated the Freak's leader, it didn't take much to make him talk: <br><br>'This wouldn't have had to happen if your fascist Arachnos employers hadn't sent guys against us. You crashed our power grid! You hacked our meat doctors' medical computer! You cut our pirated cable TV! And you stole the formula for our drug, Excelsior!  Oh, this ain't over!  Just wait until Dreck hears about this!  We'll roll over those Arachnos jerks like a wave of steel! And anyone who stands with them, including you!'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BruceTalks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3112436409" "Captain Braun talks"
// DetailString :
"P1413688482" "It took some work, but you were able to get a name out of Captain Braun: 'Agent Glenn Sampson'. It should be all you need."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SampsonTalks 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4114588873" "Agent Sampson tells all"
// DetailString :
"P4056700349" "Agent Sampson was smart enough to talk without any extra persuasion: <br><br>'Whoa, there! No need to get all nasty. I'll talk! I'll sing, I'll dance, whatever you want. I heard that we had a deep-cover guy inside Arachnos who was supposed to be infiltrating other groups' computer networks and pinning it on Arachnos. That way, Longbow gets the information and Arachnos takes the heat. I knew that there were people who'd pay for a share of that information, so I found a way to get it. The agent is leaving his information at specific drop points according to a schedule. I just made sure I was on the recover team, and made copies. I'll tell you where to go to intercept the next the next drop. If you're lucky, you can make it there before Longbow.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - GWInfo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P425277066" "A partial dossier on Ghost Widow"
// DetailString :
"P3833987911" "Though not complete, this file contains some interesting information about Ghost Widow, a member of Lord Recluse's inner circle: <br><br> Name: Ghost Widow<br>Real Name: Unknown <br>Power Source: Magic (Ghost)<br>Associates: Wretch <br><br>While I have not been able to determine her original identity, Ghost Widow began as a member of the Night Widows, Arachnos's semi-cultish group of female assassins and mystics. She was likely killed in action during Lord Recluse's take-over of the Rogue Isles, but returned as a spectral undead apparition. The process of dying has only increased her powers, and she quickly rose to lead the Widows. She can manifest herself physically at will, and affect the physical world with a variety of supernatural abilities. If she is dispersed she can reform herself over time, making her potentially unstoppable. She seems concerned with controlling other ghostly entities, so this may point to a potential weakness. <br>How she returned from the dead is unknown, though after seeing her, I believe that the Legacy Chain's theory is correct: she returned of her own free will as a spectre, but bound to the fortunes of Arachnos. She is tremendously loyal to Arachnos and personally loyal to Lord Recluse, though we don't know the reason or origin of this loyalty. She is often accompanied by Wretch, a former Arachnos soldier who we believe was scarred and horribly mutated in the same incident that caused Ghost Widow's original demise.' <br><br>With the rest of these dossiers, it may be possible to trace back the location and identity of the spy who compiled these reports."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BSInfo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2337300270" "A partial dossier on Black Scorpion"
// DetailString :
"P3011075026" "Though not complete, this file contains some interesting information about Black Scorpion, a member of Lord Recluse's inner circle: <br><br>'Name: Black Scorpion <br>Real Name: Ernesto Rodriguez <br>Power Source: Technology (Powered Armor/Cybernetics) <br>Associates: Silver Mantis <br>Ernesto began his career as a mercenary, and a very good one. He was highly paid for his ability to eliminate super powered threats to his employers with conventional troops. After he acquired the Black Scorpion armor, he was nearly unstoppable. He was hired by Lord Recluse and brought into Arachnos shortly afterwards, but I have reason to believe that they've worked together in the past. Since he's been brought into Arachnos, Ernesto has continued to improve the armor, as well as modify himself with cybernetic implants. He's probably encouraged in the latter by Silver Mantis, a close associate of his who is herself heavily cybernetically augmented. <br><br>I have not been able to ascertain how Rodriguez attained the Black Scorpion suit, but the name 'Dr. Quatrexin' has come up several times. Rodriguez's first appearance as Black Scorpion would roughly match the time of Dr. Quatrexin's disappearance several years ago in the American Southwest. Recommend we try to locate Quatrexin immediately to find weakness in the Black Scorpion Suit.' <br><br>With the rest of these dossiers, it may be possible to trace back the location and identity of the spy who compiled these reports."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SIInfo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P846149649" "A partial dossier on Sirocco"
// DetailString :
"P60398422" "Though not complete, this file contains some interesting information about Sirocco, a member of Lord Recluse's inner circle: <br><br>'Name: Sirocco <br>Real Name: Imad Malak <br>Power Source: Magic (Artifacts) <br>Assosciates: Ice Mistral <br><br>Malak is a real mystery. As far as I can tell, he began as a freedom fighter against a tyrannical regime in the Middle East, then gained the artifacts that gave him his powers and continued fighting against tyranny. He then began to slip into more questionable work, including selling off some more magical artifacts, probably from the same find. Within a few years, he was an international criminal, and near the top of Interpol's most wanted list. He joined Arachnos soon after. What no one can ascertain is why he went rogue. He still maintains some amount of honor, and has even allowed innocents to escape the line of fire before a battle. From his interaction with the young villainess Ice Mistral, some think he might be trying to reform her, though with little success. There are rumors that he may be under some kind of curse. This may be worth investigating. <br><br>Another mystery is where he got his artifacts from, but there are myths of a great hero of Arabian myth with similar powers. This mythic hero supposedly received his magic tools from a djinn called Serafina. <br><br>While Sirocco may or may not be idealogically aligned with Lord Recluse, he has never betrayed his master's trust. Whether this is due to Sirocco's personal sense of honor, mercenary ethics, or some other compulsion is unknown.' <br><br>With the rest of these dossiers, it may be possible to trace back the location and identity of the spy who compiled these reports."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CMInfo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3903071564" "A partial dossier on Cap'n Mako"
// DetailString :
"P962224695" "Though not complete, this file contains some interesting information about Cap'n Mako, a member of Lord Recluse's inner circle: <br><br>'Name: Cap'n Mako <br>Real Name: unknown <br>Power Source: Mutation (Animalistic) <br>Associates: Barracuda <br><br>Cap'n Mako's true origins are unknown. He first appeared as a modern pirate working around the Rogue Isles before Lord Recluse claimed them. Mako and his crew initially fought against Lord Recluse's forces during the take-over, but was either coerced or bought off and joined Arachnos. He's been more than happy to continue working in Lord Recluse's employ since then. Recluse often uses Mako as an assassin and enforcer, sending him to make violent examples out of enemies of Arachnos. Mako's brutal murder of the original Scrapyard on the docks of Sharkhead Isle is a perfect example. Mako is a bloodthirsty predator capable of casual violence, but he still possesses a human intellect, and should not be underestimated.  <br><br>Mako has recently installed himself on Sharkhead Island. I have been unable to find out why, though he went to Sharkhead shortly after he began to associate with the villainess Barracuda. I have been unable to find out much about her origin, except that she was once human, but was altered somehow. I've heard the term 'Koralax' used, but don't know what it means.' <br><br>With the rest of these dossiers, it may be possible to trace back the location and identity of the spy who compiled these reports."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AgentLoc 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2261022311" "The Longbow Spy"
// DetailString :
"P250309921" "By putting together clues in all of the information you recovered at the drop points, you think you know the location and identity of Longbow's spy in Arachnos."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2163530551" "A Web of Intrigue"
// DetailString :
"P3065102270" "Vargas seemed upset that all he had to give you was a simple mission of revenge against the Council for an attack on Arachnos. The mission had been given to Vargas at the last minute, and he was fuming about it. The pay was good, but something seemed strange. Your suspicions were confirmed when one of the Council soldiers said that they had only attacked because a computer hacker from Arachnos had raided their systems."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1255101068" "Vargas seemed upset that all he had to give you was a simple mission of revenge against the Council for an attack on Arachnos. The mission had been given to Vargas at the last minute, and he was fuming about it. The pay was good, but something seemed strange. Your suspicions were confirmed when one of the Council soldiers said that they had only attacked because a computer hacker from Arachnos had raided their systems. <br><br>Vargas had checked into the Council's claim, but hadn't found any evidence of a scheduled computer strike against them. As you were talking, he received a call from Arbiter Leery with an urgent mission: a gang of Freakshow had over-run an Arachnos base, and Leery wanted them out. Vargas offered you the job since it would take him too long to organize a strike force. You fought the Freaks, and found out that they had attacked because their computer system had been compromised by Arachnos, too."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3419031194" "Vargas seemed upset that all he had to give you was a simple mission of revenge against the Council for an attack on Arachnos. The mission had been given to Vargas at the last minute, and he was fuming about it. The pay was good, but something seemed strange. Your suspicions were confirmed when one of the Council soldiers said that they had only attacked because a computer hacker from Arachnos had raided their systems. <br><br>Vargas had checked into the Council's claim, but hadn't found any evidence of a scheduled computer strike against them. As you were talking, he received a call from Arbiter Leery with an urgent mission: a gang of Freakshow had over-run an Arachnos base, and Leery wanted them out. Vargas offered you the job since it would take him too long to organize a strike force. You fought the Freaks, and found out that they had attacked because their computer system had been compromised by Arachnos, too. <br><br>It was time to stop being reactive. Vargas had heard through a friend of his in the Sky Raiders about a Longbow agent who sold information on the side, and was now offering some of the information that had been stolen from the Council and the Freakshow. If that information had gotten into the hands of a Longbow agent, then there might be some connection between Longbow and the attacks on Arachnos. The only way to find the renegade Longbow agent was to get the information from Vargas's old friend, Captain Braun. It wasn't pleasant, but you got the information."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2887123039" "Vargas seemed upset that all he had to give you was a simple mission of revenge against the Council for an attack on Arachnos. The mission had been given to Vargas at the last minute, and he was fuming about it. The pay was good, but something seemed strange. Your suspicions were confirmed when one of the Council soldiers said that they had only attacked because a computer hacker from Arachnos had raided their systems. <br><br>Vargas had checked into the Council's claim, but hadn't found any evidence of a scheduled computer strike against them. As you were talking, he received a call from Arbiter Leery with an urgent mission: A gang of Freakshow had over-run an Arachnos base, and Leery wanted them out. Vargas offered you the job, since it would take him too long to organize a strike force. You fought the Freaks, and found out that they had attacked because their computer system had been compromised by Arachnos, too. <br><br>It was time to stop being reactive. Vargas had heard through a friend of his in the Sky Raiders about a Longbow agent who sold information on the side, and was now offering some of the information that had been stolen from the Council and the Freakshow. If that information had gotten into the hands of a Longbow agent, then there might be some connection between Longbow and the attacks on Arachnos. The only way to find the renegade Longbow agent was to get the information from Vargas's old friend, Captain Braun. It wasn't pleasant, but you got the information. <br><br>You moved swiftly, and caught Glenn Sampson, the renegade Longbow agent. He was willing to talk to spare his life, and told where he had gotten the information he was currently selling. It seems that Longbow had an agent inside Arachnos to hack other groups and direct the blame on them. Sampson told you where the agent was dropping off the next batch of information. You captured the info, and with it were able to find the Agent's identity and where he was stationed."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission5Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2042128906" "Vargas seemed upset that all he had to give you was a simple mission of revenge against the Council for an attack on Arachnos. The mission had been given to Vargas at the last minute, and he was fuming about it. The pay was good, but something seemed strange. Your suspicions were confirmed when one of the Council soldiers said that they had only attacked because a computer hacker from Arachnos had raided their systems. <br><br>Vargas had checked into the Council's claim, but hadn't found any evidence of a scheduled computer strike against them. As you were talking, he received a call from Arbiter Leery with an urgent mission: a gang of Freakshow had over-run an Arachnos base, and Leery wanted them out. Vargas offered you the job since it would take him too long to organize a strike force. You fought the Freaks, and found out that they had attacked because their computer system had been compromised by Arachnos, too. <br><br>It was time to stop being reactive. Vargas had heard through a friend of his in the Sky Raiders about a Longbow agent who sold information on the side, and was now offering some of the information that had been stolen from the Council and the Freakshow. If that information had gotten into the hands of a Longbow agent, then there might be some connection between Longbow and the attacks on Arachnos. The only way to find the renegade Longbow agent was to get the information from Vargas's old friend, Captain Braun. It wasn't pleasant, but you got the information. <br><br>You moved swiftly, and caught Glenn Sampson, the renegade Longbow agent. He was willing to talk to spare his life, and told you where he had gotten the information he was currently selling. It seems that Longbow had an agent inside Arachnos to hack other groups and direct the blame on them. Sampson told you where the agent was dropping off the next batch of information. You captured the info, and with it were able to find the Agent's identity and where he was stationed. <br><br>Vargas went above Arbiter Leery and got a full sanction from Arbiter Daos to capture the Longbow Spy by any means necessary. Since the infiltration couldn't be revealed, Vargas asked you to do it. You caught Longbow's spy, Agent Caspian, inside the Arachnos base where he had secured himself."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL4_Vargas_StoryArc1_SouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1451125605" "A Longbow codebook"
// tDetailString :
"P3831861583" "Though the codes in this book are now out of date, it serves as a reminder of the escapade where you captured it from a Longbow underwater base. An escapade you like to remember as: <br><br>A Web of Intrigue <br><br>When it all began, Vargas seemed upset that all he had to give you was a simple mission of revenge against the Council for an attack on Arachnos. The mission had been given to Vargas at the last minute, and he was fuming about it. The pay was good, but something seemed strange. Your suspicions were confirmed when one of the Council soldiers said that they had only attacked because a computer hacker from Arachnos had raided their systems. <br><br>Vargas had checked into the Council's claim, but hadn't found any evidence of a scheduled computer strike against them. As you were talking, he received a call from Arbiter Leery with an urgent mission: a gang of Freakshow had over-run an Arachnos base, and Leery wanted them out. Vargas offered you the job since it would take him too long to organize a strike force. You fought the Freaks, and found out that they had attacked because their computer system had been compromised by Arachnos, too. <br><br>It was time to stop being reactive. Vargas had heard through a friend of his in the Sky Raiders about a Longbow agent who sold information on the side, and was now offering some of the information that had been stolen from the Council and the Freakshow. If that information had gotten into the hands of a Longbow agent, then there might be some connection between Longbow and the attacks on Arachnos. The only way to find the renegade Longbow agent was to get the information from Vargas's old friend, Captain Braun. It wasn't pleasant, but you got the information. <br><br>You moved swiftly and caught Glenn Sampson, the renegade Longbow agent. He was willing to talk to spare his life, and told you where he had gotten the information he was currently selling. It seems that Longbow had an agent inside Arachnos to hack other groups and direct the blame on them. Sampson told you where the agent was dropping off the next batch of information. You captured the info, and with it were able to find the Agent's identity and where he was stationed. <br><br>Vargas went above Arbiter Leery and got a full sanction from Arbiter Daos to capture the Longbow Spy by any means necessary. Since the infiltration couldn't be revealed, Vargas asked you to do it. You caught Longbow's spy, Agent Caspian, inside the Arachnos base where he had secured himself. <br><br>Caspian talked in interrogation, and revealed the location of a Longbow underwater base. Vargas decided to take the initiative, and hired you to take it out before someone else could steal his thunder. You entered the underwater base by mini-sub using codes extracted from Caspian. You forced a captured technician to lower the base's computer security, defeated the security chief who was apparently Caspian's older brother, and captured the base commander. The base fell, and Longbow's spy operations were severely set back. <br><br>In the aftermath, Vargas is on the fast track to promotion, and promised to speak your praises far and wide. Somehow, you're not counting on that promise too much. But you were well paid, and Longbow took a big fall. Not bad for some dishonest work."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P653464345" "Okay, I have something for you, but, well, it's not up to someone of your caliber. It's grunt work, and they gave it to me because someone, and I'm not entirely sure who, is trying to sandbag me. Weigh me down with menial tasks. Can you believe it? Someone like me, someone destined for greatness, for the highest ranks. Well, it's a good thing I have resources. I have allies. Allies like you. So, here's the deal: the Council raided one of our bases, and now I have to organize a strike on the base they came from. Getting together forces and authorizing expenditures will take me half a week, and I don't have time for that. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Or, I can ask you to handle this for me. Not as a favor. You're a professional, I wouldn't do that to you. It'll be full pay for you and any one you choose. Full pay for all of you. I just need this situation dealt with.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2146334586" "Take out Council base in retaliation"
// SendOffString :
"P3232811362" "Take out the base. Take out everyone in the base. These Council guys, I swear, what is it with them? I don't know why Lord Recluse doesn't just crush them. Maybe it's because he used to work with them way back in the thirties. And I'm not criticizing Lord Recluse, let me make that clear, but if that's his reason, I think he should reconsider it. Sentiment, as a concept, is outmoded. Just like loyalty or morality, it only holds you back."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1451734399" "Defeat all Council in base"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4289365706" "{VillainName}, you're a professional. You know what to do. I trust you to do this."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3539499397" "Arachnos and the Council fight a lot, but something seems strange this time."

