// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3336693570" "You defeated the Freaks and disarmed the bombs."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P646118634" "You were unable to stop the Freakshow in time!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P419075957" "He said what? That they were retaliating against us? There wasn't any plans against the Freakshow. Nothing had been allocated, nothing had been authorized. It wasn't on any org charts or flowcharts or the minutes of any meetings. It's all coming out of nowhere. Or is it? I got a sneaking suspicion that this is connected to that Council attack. <br><br>Those Freakshow, I just don't get those guys. Singing and dancing while setting bombs? Aren't they taking this seriously? Who did this guy think he was, the music man? I swear, anything goes with those guys."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1998085005" "We've been able to mitigate the damage, but the higher ups are real upset. They've taken the damage done out of your pay. I argued against it because I understand how these situations can escalate, but there was nothing I could do. <br><br>But let's not concentrate on that. I found out why the Freaks were attacking. It seems that they thought we'd gone after them first. They thought we'd hacked into their computers, stole the designs for their drugs, shut off their generators, and scrambled their satellite TV. But as far as I can tell, there weren't any plans to do anything like that to the Freakshow on the table."

